@* UserDetail.razor — Phase 6.3 (Phase 6.6 — group UI rework + activate/deactivate + reset password)

   Staff-facing user detail page at route `/Admin/Users/{Id:guid}`. Reached
   from the /Admin/Users list page (Phase 6.1) by clicking the "View
   details" (visibility) icon in the actions column. Page-level gate is
   [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager,Employee")] — same as the list page —
   and the backend GetUserByIdQueryHandler additionally allows Employee
   to view any user (but strips GroupName for non-Customer targets).
   Customers/ReadOnly can only view their own profile via this same route
   (the handler enforces that defense-in-depth by returning a generic
   "not found" for other users).

   BACKEND CONTRACT:
     - Load: GetUserByIdQuery { UserId } → Result<UserDto>
       - Returns the UserDto (Id, WorkerId, FullName, Gender, GroupName?,
         IsActive, Email? [currently always null — TODO in handler], Roles list).
       - GroupName is populated for Admin/Manager viewers (any target) AND
         for Employee viewers when the target is a Customer. Otherwise null.
       - Returns Result.Failure("User '...' was not found.") for both
         genuinely-missing users AND viewers-not-allowed-to-see (the
         canonical "never leak existence" pattern, same as GetSaleByIdQuery).
     - Edit FullName: UpdateUserFullNameCommand(UserId, NewFullName) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]. Validator: NewFullName non-empty,
         ≤ 200 chars.
     - Assign role: AssignUserRoleCommand(UserId, Role) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Admin)]. Validator: Role must be one of
         {Admin, Manager, Employee, ReadOnly, Customer}.
     - Remove role: RemoveUserRoleCommand(UserId, Role) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Admin)]. Handler rejects self-removal of own Admin
         role (defense-in-depth). Validator: same as Assign.
     - Assign to group: AssignUserToGroupCommand(UserId, GroupName) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Employee, Manager, Admin)]. Handler enforces caller-
         scope rules: Admin → any target; Manager → Employee/Customer
         (not self, not other managers/admins); Employee → Customer only
         (not self, not other employees/managers/admins). Validator:
         GroupName non-empty, ≤ 100 chars.
     - Remove from group: RemoveUserFromGroupCommand(UserId) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]. Validator: UserId non-empty.
     - Activate: ActivateUserCommand(UserId) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]. Handler: Manager scope is
         Employee/Customer (not self, not other managers/admins/read-onlys).
         Self-activation is rejected.
     - Deactivate: DeactivateUserCommand(UserId) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]. Same scope as Activate.
     - Reset password: ResetUserPasswordCommand(UserId, NewPassword) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Admin)]. Identity complexity rules apply.

   LAYOUT (responsive — mirrors SaleDetail.razor's 12-col grid):
     Desktop / tablet (≥992px): two columns
       Left  (8/12): profile card + roles card + group card
       Right (4/12): sticky action panel (help + role-scope info + error)
     Mobile (<992px): single column, action panel collapses to top

   ROLE-RESOLUTION PATTERN:
     _isAdmin, _isManager, _isEmployee, _currentUserId are computed in
     OnInitializedAsync via AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync()
     — NOT via ICurrentUserService.IsInRole (which returns false for
     everyone in interactive Blazor Server mode because HttpContext is
     null over the SignalR circuit). Same pattern as AdminUsers.razor
     (Phase 6.1) and SaleDetail.razor (Phase 4.3). See those files'
     header comments for the full rationale. The Wolverine command
     handlers ALSO enforce [RequireRoles] server-side as defense-in-depth.

   ROLE-SCOPE RULES (Phase 6.6 — applied per-action via CanActivate,
     CanChangeGroup, CanResetPassword):

     ACTIVATE / DEACTIVATE (ActivateUserCommand / DeactivateUserCommand):
       - Admin    → anyone except self (handler rejects self).
       - Manager  → Employee or Customer targets, NOT self, NOT other
                    managers/admins/read-onlys.
       - Employee → cannot activate/deactivate anyone (command is
                    [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]).

     CHANGE GROUP (AssignUserToGroupCommand):
       - Admin    → anyone (including self, though admins don't have groups).
       - Manager  → Employee or Customer targets, NOT self, NOT other
                    managers/admins/read-onlys.
       - Employee → Customer targets only, NOT self, NOT other
                    employees/managers/admins/read-onlys.

     RESET PASSWORD (ResetUserPasswordCommand):
       - Admin only. Hidden from Managers and Employees.

   UX PATTERNS:
     - Edit FullName: opens an in-page modal dialog (NOT a browser JS prompt
       — the modal gives us proper labels, validation messaging, and
       Save/Cancel buttons). The modal markup lives at the bottom of this
       file.
     - Assign role: RadzenDropDown (TValue=string, primitive key — matches
       AdminUsers.razor's activity-filter pattern, NOT the complex-object
       binding pattern that bit us in CreateUser.razor Phase 6.2). Dropdown
       options are filtered to remove roles the user already has, AND to
       remove Customer (Customer is implicit — set at creation time, not
       assignable post-creation from this UI).
     - Remove role: small icon button per assigned role. Hidden on the
       current user's own Admin role (handler rejects this as
       defense-in-depth, but hiding the button is better UX — same pattern
       as AdminUsers.razor hiding self-Deactivate).
     - Change group / Assign to group (Phase 6.6 rework): the green button
       is labeled "Change group" when the user has a group, or "Assign to
       group" when they don't. Clicking it opens an inline panel with the
       SAME UI as CreateUser.razor's group-name field — two toggle cards
       (Existing / New), a 2-column grid of existing-group buttons in
       Existing mode, and a textbox in New mode. Save dispatches
       AssignUserToGroupCommand. Only shown when CanChangeGroup returns
       true for the current viewer + target.
     - Remove from group: direct button click (with a JS confirm() because
       it's destructive — removes the user's purchase-limit group). Only
       shown when the user has a group AND the viewer can change the group
       (CanChangeGroup).
     - Activate / Deactivate: a button in the action panel (right column).
       Shows "Deactivate" when the user is active, "Activate" when inactive.
       Hidden when _isViewingSelf (handler also rejects self-activation).
       Hidden entirely when CanActivate returns false.
     - Reset password: a button in the action panel (Admin only, not self).
       Opens an in-page modal (same style as the Edit FullName modal) with
       a password input + show/hide toggle + Save/Cancel.
     - All actions are wrapped in ExecuteActionAsync (mirrors SaleDetail)
       which: sets _isBusy, clears _actionError, dispatches, toasts on
       success/failure, reloads the user on success.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All button clicks are async event handlers
     that dispatch commands via Wolverine. The Blazor circuit's anti-forgery
     token is established at circuit start. (Same as SaleDetail.razor.) *@

@page "/Admin/Users/{Id:guid}"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager,Employee")]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Users.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Queries.GetUserById
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Queries.GetAllGroupNames
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.UpdateUserFullName
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.AssignUserRole
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.RemoveUserRole
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.AssignUserToGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.RemoveUserFromGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.ActivateUser
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.DeactivateUser
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.ResetUserPassword
@using TakOne.Domain.Users
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<UserDetail> Loc
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<PageTitle>@(_user is null ? Loc["PageTitle"] : $"{_user.WorkerId} — {Loc["PageTitle"]}")</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Layout — 12-col grid on desktop/tablet, stacks on mobile.
                                       Left = profile + roles + group cards (wider); right = sticky action panel.
                                       Mirrors SaleDetail.razor's .detail-grid structure. */
            .detail-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 1.5rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .detail-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1rem;
                }
                    /* On mobile, action panel comes FIRST so help + role-scope
                                               context is visible before the user scrolls to the cards. */
                    .detail-grid .detail-action-panel {
                        order: -1;
                    }
            }

            /* Page header — worker ID (monospace) + active badge inline. */
            .detail-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 1rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            .detail-worker-id {
                font-family: var(--rz-monospace-font-family, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
                font-size: 1.6rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                margin: 0;
                line-height: 1.2;
            }

            /* Breadcrumb (same style as SaleDetail.razor). */
            .breadcrumb {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            }

                .breadcrumb a {
                    color: var(--rz-primary);
                    text-decoration: none;
                }

                    .breadcrumb a:hover {
                        text-decoration: underline;
                    }

            .crumb-sep {
                opacity: 0.6;
            }

            .crumb-current {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            /* Scope badge (large) in the action panel header — same shape
                                       as SaleDetail.razor's .status-badge-large. */
            .status-badge-large {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
                border-radius: 9999px;
                font-size: 1rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                min-width: 120px;
                justify-content: center;
            }

            /* Per-scope background colors (semantic):
                                       - Admin   → primary  (highest privilege — visually distinct)
                                       - Manager → info     (mid privilege)
                                       - Viewer  → base     (read-only) */
            .scope-bg-admin {
                background: rgba(63, 81, 181, 0.18);
                color: #1a237e;
            }

            .scope-bg-manager {
                background: rgba(33, 150, 243, 0.18);
                color: #0d47a1;
            }

            .scope-bg-viewer {
                background: rgba(158, 158, 158, 0.18);
                color: #424242;
            }

            /* Sticky action panel on desktop. */
            @@media (min-width: 993px) {
                .detail-action-panel {
                    position: sticky;
                    top: 1rem;
                }
            }

            /* Profile card — 2-column field grid (label + value). */
            .profile-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(120px, 1fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
                gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
                align-items: baseline;
            }

            .profile-label {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            .profile-value {
                font-weight: 500;
                word-break: break-word;
            }

            .profile-value-mono {
                font-family: var(--rz-monospace-font-family, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
                font-weight: 600;
            }

            .profile-value-muted {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            /* Role badges list — horizontal flex wrap with remove buttons. */
            .role-list {
                display: flex;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                align-items: center;
            }

            .role-item {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
            }

            .role-remove-btn {
                cursor: pointer;
                background: transparent;
                border: none;
                color: inherit;
                opacity: 0.7;
                padding: 0;
                line-height: 1;
                font-size: 1rem;
            }

                .role-remove-btn:hover {
                    opacity: 1;
                }

            .role-empty {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            /* Inline action forms — assign role / assign group rows. */
            .inline-form {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                align-items: stretch;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
                margin-top: 0.75rem;
            }

                .inline-form .rz-dropdown {
                    flex: 1 1 180px;
                    min-width: 160px;
                }

            /* ── Group change panel (Phase 6.6) ──
                           Mirrors CreateUser.razor's group-name UI: two toggle cards
                           (Existing / New) + a 2-column grid of existing-group buttons
                           (Existing mode) OR a textbox (New mode). The toggle cards
                           use the same .toggle-option / .is-selected pattern as
                           CreateUser.razor's .usertype-option, so the visual style
                           is identical. */
            .toggle-option {
                transition: background-color 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;
            }

                .toggle-option.is-selected {
                    background-color: var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(var(--rz-primary-rgb, 67, 56, 202), 0.08));
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary) !important;
                }

            .toggle-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

                .toggle-row .toggle-option {
                    flex: 1 1 200px;
                    min-width: 200px;
                }

            .group-list {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
                gap: 0.5rem;
            }

            .group-change-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                margin-top: 0.75rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            /* Help panel bullets. */
            .help-list {
                margin: 0;
                padding-left: 1.25rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                line-height: 1.55;
            }

                .help-list li {
                    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
                }

            /* ── Edit Full Name modal ──
                                       Inline modal overlay + dialog. Renders above all other
                                       content via position:fixed + z-index. Backdrop is a
                                       semi-transparent dark layer that dims the underlying page
                                       (matches Radzen Dialog's visual weight). The dialog itself
                                       is a Radzen-styled card with max-width to keep it compact
                                       on desktop and full-width (minus margins) on mobile. */
            .modal-overlay {
                position: fixed;
                inset: 0;
                background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                z-index: 1050;
                padding: 1rem;
                /* Smooth open transition. */
                animation: modal-fade-in 0.15s ease-out;
            }

            @@keyframes modal-fade-in {
                from {
                    opacity: 0;
                }

                to {
                    opacity: 1;
                }
            }

            .modal-dialog {
                background: var(--rz-background-color, #fff);
                border-radius: 8px;
                box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
                width: 100%;
                max-width: 480px;
                max-height: calc(100vh - 2rem);
                overflow-y: auto;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                animation: modal-slide-up 0.2s ease-out;
            }

            @@keyframes modal-slide-up {
                from {
                    transform: translateY(20px);
                    opacity: 0;
                }

                to {
                    transform: translateY(0);
                    opacity: 1;
                }
            }

            .modal-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: space-between;
                padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
                border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08));
            }

            .modal-title {
                margin: 0;
                font-size: 1.125rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                color: var(--rz-text-color, #212121);
            }

            .modal-close-btn {
                background: transparent;
                border: none;
                cursor: pointer;
                padding: 0.25rem;
                line-height: 1;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 1.25rem;
                border-radius: 4px;
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
            }

                .modal-close-btn:hover:not(:disabled) {
                    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
                    color: var(--rz-text-color);
                }

                .modal-close-btn:disabled {
                    opacity: 0.5;
                    cursor: not-allowed;
                }

            .modal-body {
                padding: 1.25rem;
                flex: 1 1 auto;
            }

            .modal-body-text {
                margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.9375rem;
                line-height: 1.5;
            }

            .modal-label {
                display: block;
                margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            .modal-validation {
                min-height: 1.25rem;
                margin-top: 0.5rem;
                font-size: 0.8125rem;
            }

            .modal-validation-error {
                color: var(--rz-danger, #f44336);
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.25rem;
            }

            .modal-footer {
                display: flex;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
                border-top: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08));
            }

            /* On small screens, modal footer buttons stretch full-width
                                       and stack vertically for easier thumb-tapping. */
            @@media (max-width: 576px) {
                .modal-footer {
                    flex-direction: column-reverse;
                }

                    .modal-footer .rz-button {
                        width: 100%;
                    }
            }

            /* Password row inside the Reset Password modal — textbox on
                           the left (flex-grow), show/hide toggle button on the right. */
            .modal-password-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                align-items: stretch;
            }

                .modal-password-row .modal-password-field {
                    flex: 1 1 auto;
                    min-width: 0;
                }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Back button ──
       Returns to /Admin/Users. forceLoad:false preserves the Blazor circuit. *@
    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToList"]"
                  Icon="arrow_back"
                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                  Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Users", forceLoad: false))" />

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Error state ── *@
    else if (_loadError is not null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadUserAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Not found ──
       The handler returns Result.Failure with a "not found" message for
       both genuinely-missing users AND users the caller isn't allowed
       to see (defense-in-depth — never leak existence). Either way, the
       user sees the same friendly message. Same pattern as SaleDetail.razor. *@
    else if (_user is null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["NotFoundTitle"]"
                     Text="@Loc["NotFoundMessage"]"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Main content ── *@
    else
    {
        <div class="detail-grid">
            @* LEFT — profile + roles + group cards *@
            <div>
                @* Breadcrumb: Manage users / [Worker ID] *@
                <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="breadcrumb" Style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                    <a href="/Admin/Users">@Loc["BreadcrumbUsers"]</a>
                    <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
                    <span class="crumb-current">@_user.WorkerId</span>
                </nav>

                @* Page header — worker ID + active badge inline *@
                <div class="detail-header" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    <h1 class="detail-worker-id">@_user.WorkerId</h1>
                    @if (_user.IsActive)
                    {
                        <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusActive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Success" IsPill="true" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusInactive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light" IsPill="true" />
                    }
                </div>

                @* ── Profile card ──
                   Read-only identity fields. FullName has an inline "Edit"
                   button that opens an in-page modal dialog (NOT a browser
                   JS prompt — the modal gives us proper labels, validation
                   messaging, and Save/Cancel buttons). The modal markup
                   lives at the bottom of this file. Group is shown when
                   the handler returned a non-null GroupName (Admin/Manager
                   viewers see it for any user; Employee viewers see it
                   only for Customer targets — see GetUserByIdQueryHandler
                   step 4). The dedicated Group card below provides the
                   change-group UI when CanChangeGroup is true. *@
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    <RadzenText Text="@Loc["ProfileCardTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 600;" />

                    <div class="profile-grid">
                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColWorkerId"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value profile-value-mono">@_user.WorkerId</div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColFullName"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">
                            @_user.FullName
                            @if (_canEditFullName)
                            {
                                <RadzenButton Icon="edit"
                                              Text="@Loc["ActionEditFullName"]"
                                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Info"
                                              Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                              Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                              Click="@HandleEditFullNameAsync"
                                              Style="margin-left: 0.5rem;" />
                            }
                        </div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColGender"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">@GetGenderLabel(_user.Gender)</div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColStatus"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">
                            @if (_user.IsActive)
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusActive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Success" IsPill="true" />
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusInactive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light" IsPill="true" />
                            }
                        </div>

                        @* Email is currently always null in the DTO (TODO
                           in handler — IUserAccountService has no GetEmailAsync
                           yet). When the handler is extended, this row will
                           light up automatically without UI changes. *@
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.Email))
                        {
                            <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColEmail"]</div>
                            <div class="profile-value profile-value-mono">@_user.Email</div>
                        }

                        @* Group row — shown when the viewer can change this
                           user's group (CanChangeGroup) OR when the handler
                           returned a non-null GroupName (which happens for
                           Admin/Manager viewers regardless of whether the
                           user has a group). When GroupName is null AND
                           CanChangeGroup is false, the target is either
                           a non-Customer (Employee viewer) or the viewer's
                           own profile (Customer viewer) — in both cases,
                           hiding the row is correct. The dedicated Group
                           card below provides the change-group UI when
                           CanChangeGroup returns true. *@
                        @if (CanChangeGroup() || !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName))
                        {
                            <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColGroup"]</div>
                            <div class="profile-value">
                                @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName))
                                {
                                    <span class="profile-value-muted">@Loc["GroupNone"]</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@_user.GroupName" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Base" IsPill="true" />
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                </RadzenCard>

                @* ── Roles card ──
                   Shows the user's currently-assigned ASP.NET Identity roles.

                   SELF-ROLE-MANAGEMENT GUARD:
                   When an admin views their OWN detail page, the entire
                   "Assign role" + "Remove role" UI is hidden and replaced
                   with an info alert. This is intentional UX — admins CAN
                   change the roles of OTHER admins (including removing
                   Admin from another admin), but they CANNOT modify their
                   own roles from this page. The backend handler
                   (RemoveUserRoleCommandHandler) ALSO rejects self-Admin-
                   removal as defense-in-depth; the UI guard just makes
                   this discoverable instead of letting the admin click
                   and get an error toast.

                   Why hide rather than disable: the admin's own roles are
                   effectively read-only from this page (any change to
                   their own roles would have to come from another admin's
                   session). Showing disabled buttons would imply "you
                   almost can" — misleading. A clean read-only view with
                   an explanatory alert is more honest. Same pattern used
                   by AdminUsers.razor for the self-Deactivate button.

                   DROPDOWN BINDING (Phase 6.3 fix):
                   Originally used RadzenDropDown TValue="string" with
                   Data=List<RoleOption> + TextProperty/ValueProperty.
                   That produced "Unable to cast RoleOption to String"
                   inside Radzen.DropDownBase.SelectItem — Radzen 11.1.7's
                   code path for primitive TValue + complex items does not
                   reliably honor ValueProperty when the user clicks an
                   item, and falls back to item.ToString(), producing the
                   garbage label "TakOne.WebUI.Components.Pages.UserDetail+RoleOption".

                   Fix: Data is now List<string> (raw role constants like
                   "Admin", "Manager", ...). The dropdown value IS the
                   role string — no casting needed. An ItemTemplate
                   renders the localized label (GetRoleLabel) so the user
                   sees translated text. Same primitive-binding pattern
                   as AdminUsers.razor's activity-filter dropdown. *@
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    <RadzenText Text="@Loc["RolesCardTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 600;" />

                    @if (_user.Roles.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <div class="role-empty">@Loc["NoRoles"]</div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="role-list">
                            @foreach (var role in _user.Roles)
                            {
                                <span class="role-item">
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@GetRoleLabel(role)"
                                                 BadgeStyle="@GetRoleBadgeStyle(role)"
                                                 IsPill="true" />
                                    @* Remove button — hidden when:
                                          (a) viewer can't manage roles, OR
                                          (b) the viewer is viewing their OWN page
                                              (entire self-role block is hidden
                                              below — but this belt-and-suspenders
                                              check guards against any edge case
                                              where the markup below is shown but
                                              the per-role button shouldn't be), OR
                                          (c) it's the viewer's own Admin role
                                              (handler also rejects this — but
                                              since (b) already covers self, this
                                              is redundant defense-in-depth). *@
                                    @if (_canManageRoles && !_isViewingSelf && !(_currentUserId == _user.Id && role == Roles.Admin))
                                    {
                                        <button type="button"
                                                class="role-remove-btn"
                                                title="@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActionRemoveRoleTitle"], GetRoleLabel(role))"
                                                aria-label="@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActionRemoveRoleTitle"], GetRoleLabel(role))"
                                                disabled="@_isBusy"
                                                @onclick="@(() => HandleRemoveRoleAsync(role))">
                                            <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                                        </button>
                                    }
                                </span>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }

                    @* ── Role-management action row ──
                       Three states:
                         1. Viewer can manage roles AND is NOT viewing self:
                            show Assign dropdown + button.
                         2. Viewer can manage roles AND IS viewing self:
                            show info alert explaining self-modification is
                            not allowed.
                         3. Viewer cannot manage roles (Manager/Employee):
                            show hint that role management is Admin-only. *@
                    @if (_canManageRoles && !_isViewingSelf)
                    {
                        <div class="inline-form">
                            <RadzenDropDown TValue="string"
                                            Data="@_assignableRoles"
                                            @bind-Value="_selectedRoleToAdd"
                                            Placeholder="@Loc["RoleSelectPlaceholder"]"
                                            Style="flex: 1 1 180px; min-width: 160px;"
                                            Disabled="@(_isBusy || _assignableRoles.Count == 0)">
                                <Template Context="roleItem">
                                    @GetRoleLabel((string)roleItem)
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDropDown>
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionAssignRole"]"
                                          Icon="add"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                          Disabled="@(_isBusy || string.IsNullOrEmpty(_selectedRoleToAdd))"
                                          Click="@HandleAssignRoleAsync" />
                        </div>
                        @if (_assignableRoles.Count == 0)
                        {
                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["AllRolesAlreadyAssigned"]"
                                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["RolesHelpText"]"
                                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
                        }
                    }
                    else if (_canManageRoles && _isViewingSelf)
                    {
                        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["CannotModifyOwnRolesTitle"]"
                                     Text="@Loc["CannotModifyOwnRolesBody"]"
                                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Info"
                                     Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                     ShowIcon="true"
                                     Style="margin-top: 0.75rem;" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["RolesManagerOnlyHint"]"
                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
                    }
                </RadzenCard>

                @* ── Group card ──
                   Visibility: shown when the viewer can change this user's
                   group (CanChangeGroup). The card shows the user's current
                   group, a green "Change group" or "Assign to group" button
                   (label depends on whether a group is currently set), and
                   — when the button is clicked — an inline panel with the
                   SAME UI as CreateUser.razor's group-name field (two
                   toggle cards Existing/New + grid of existing-group buttons
                   OR a textbox for a new name + Save/Cancel).

                   The "Remove from group" button is shown only when the
                   user already has a group AND the viewer can change it.
                   Removal dispatches RemoveUserFromGroupCommand (which is
                   [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)] — Employees can't remove
                   a group, only change it; the handler rejects Employee
                   callers as defense-in-depth). For Employee viewers, the
                   Remove button is hidden.

                   ROLE SCOPE (per user spec, Phase 6.6):
                     - Admin    → CanChangeGroup = true for everyone (incl. self).
                     - Manager  → CanChangeGroup = true for Employee/Customer
                                  targets (not self, not other managers/admins).
                     - Employee → CanChangeGroup = true for Customer targets only
                                  (not self, not other employees/managers/admins).
                   The server-side AssignUserToGroupCommandHandler enforces
                   the same rule as defense-in-depth against tampered requests. *@
                @if (CanChangeGroup())
                {
                    <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["GroupCardTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 600;" />

                        <div class="profile-grid">
                            <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColCurrentGroup"]</div>
                            <div class="profile-value">
                                @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName))
                                {
                                    <span class="profile-value-muted">@Loc["GroupNone"]</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@_user.GroupName" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Base" IsPill="true" />
                                }
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        @if (!_isChangeGroupPanelOpen)
                        {
                            @* Default state — show the green "Change group" / "Assign to group"
                               button. Label depends on whether a group is currently set.
                               The button is green (Success) per the user's spec. *@
                            <div class="inline-form">
                                <RadzenButton Text="@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName) ? Loc["ActionAssignGroup"] : Loc["ActionChangeGroup"])"
                                              Icon="@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName) ? "group_add" : "group_edit")"
                                              IconStyle="font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1;"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Success"
                                              Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                              Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                              Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                              Click="@OpenChangeGroupPanel" />

                                @* Remove-from-group button — shown only when the user has a
                                   group AND the viewer is allowed to remove (Admin/Manager).
                                   Employees can't remove groups (command is Manager/Admin only). *@
                                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName) && (_isAdmin || _isManager))
                                {
                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionRemoveGroup"]"
                                                  Icon="group_remove"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                  Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                  Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                                  Click="@HandleRemoveGroupAsync" />
                                }
                            </div>
                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["GroupHelpText"]"
                                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            @* Expanded state — show the CreateUser-style group picker.
                               Two toggle cards (Existing / New), then the corresponding
                               panel (grid of existing groups OR a textbox for a new name),
                               then Save / Cancel buttons. Mirrors CreateUser.razor's
                               group-name field exactly. *@
                            <div class="toggle-row" Style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
                                <RadzenCard Variant="@(_groupMode == GroupMode.Existing ? Variant.Filled : Variant.Outlined)"
                                            Class="@GetToggleClass(_groupMode == GroupMode.Existing)"
                                            Style="@GetToggleBorderStyle(_groupMode == GroupMode.Existing)"
                                            @onclick="@(() => OnGroupModeChanged(GroupMode.Existing))">
                                    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="folder_open" Style="@GetToggleIconStyle(_groupMode == GroupMode.Existing)" />
                                        <div>
                                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["GroupModeExisting"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="@GetToggleTextStyle(_groupMode == GroupMode.Existing)" />
                                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["GroupModeExistingHint"]"
                                                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin: 0;" />
                                        </div>
                                    </RadzenStack>
                                </RadzenCard>

                                <RadzenCard Variant="@(_groupMode == GroupMode.New ? Variant.Filled : Variant.Outlined)"
                                            Class="@GetToggleClass(_groupMode == GroupMode.New)"
                                            Style="@GetToggleBorderStyle(_groupMode == GroupMode.New)"
                                            @onclick="@(() => OnGroupModeChanged(GroupMode.New))">
                                    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="create_new_folder" Style="@GetToggleIconStyle(_groupMode == GroupMode.New)" />
                                        <div>
                                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["GroupModeNew"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="@GetToggleTextStyle(_groupMode == GroupMode.New)" />
                                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["GroupModeNewHint"]"
                                                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin: 0;" />
                                        </div>
                                    </RadzenStack>
                                </RadzenCard>
                            </div>

                            @if (_groupMode == GroupMode.Existing)
                            {
                                <div Style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
                                    @if (!_availableGroups.Any())
                                    {
                                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                            @Loc["NoExistingGroups"]
                                        </RadzenText>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <div class="group-list">
                                            @foreach (var group in _availableGroups)
                                            {
                                                var groupName = group;  // closure capture for the lambda
                                                var isSelected = _pendingGroupName == groupName;
                                                <RadzenCard Variant="@(isSelected ? Variant.Filled : Variant.Outlined)"
                                                            Class="@GetToggleClass(isSelected)"
                                                            Style="@GetToggleBorderStyle(isSelected)"
                                                            @onclick="@(() => SelectExistingGroup(groupName))">
                                                    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center"
                                                                 JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
                                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="@(isSelected ? "check_circle" : "radio_button_unchecked")"
                                                                    Style="@GetToggleIconStyle(isSelected)" />
                                                        <RadzenText Text="@groupName" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1"
                                                                    Style="@GetToggleTextStyle(isSelected)" />
                                                    </RadzenStack>
                                                </RadzenCard>
                                            }
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                </div>
                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                                    @Loc["ExistingGroupHint"]
                                </RadzenText>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <div Style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
                                    <RadzenFormField Style="width: 100%;">
                                        <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_pendingGroupName"
                                                       Placeholder="@Loc["FieldNewGroupNamePlaceholder"]"
                                                       TValue="string"
                                                       autocomplete="off"
                                                       Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                                       Style="width: 100%;" />
                                    </RadzenFormField>
                                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                                        @Loc["NewGroupHint"]
                                    </RadzenText>
                                </div>
                            }

                            <div class="group-change-actions">
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionCancelGroupChange"]"
                                              Icon="close"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                              Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                              Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                              Click="@CancelChangeGroup" />
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionSaveGroupChange"]"
                                              Icon="check"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Success"
                                              Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                              Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                              Disabled="@(_isBusy || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_pendingGroupName))"
                                              Click="@ConfirmChangeGroupAsync" />
                            </div>
                        }
                    </RadzenCard>
                }
            </div>

            @* RIGHT — sticky action panel: scope info + inline error + help *@
            <div class="detail-action-panel">
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
                        @* Role-scope badge — at-a-glance who the viewer is. *@
                        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center;">
                            <span class="status-badge-large @GetScopeBadgeCssClass()">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="@GetScopeIcon()" />
                                @GetScopeLabel()
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        @* Scope informational alert — explains what the
                           current viewer can vs cannot do on this page.
                           Different copy per role (Admin doesn't see it;
                           Manager and Employee each see their own scope). *@
                        @if (_isEmployee && !_isAdmin && !_isManager)
                        {
                            <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["EmployeeScopeTitle"]"
                                         Text="@Loc["EmployeeScopeBody"]"
                                         AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Info"
                                         Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                         ShowIcon="true" />
                        }
                        else if (!_isAdmin)
                        {
                            <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ManagerScopeTitle"]"
                                         Text="@Loc["ManagerScopeBody"]"
                                         AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Info"
                                         Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                         ShowIcon="true" />
                        }

                        @* Inline action error — populated by ExecuteActionAsync. *@
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_actionError))
                        {
                            <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                                         Text="@_actionError"
                                         AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                         Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                         ShowIcon="true" />
                        }

                        @* ── Quick action buttons ──
                           Each is shown only when the current viewer is
                           allowed to perform that action on this user.
                           All are disabled while any action is in flight
                           (the _isBusy flag is shared). *@

                        @* Edit FullName — Admin or Manager. *@
                        @if (_canEditFullName)
                        {
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionEditFullName"]"
                                          Icon="edit"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Info"
                                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                          Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                          Click="@HandleEditFullNameAsync"
                                          Style="width: 100%;" />
                        }

                        @* Activate / Deactivate — Admin or Manager (not self).
                           Label depends on the user's current IsActive state.
                           Hidden when CanActivate returns false (covers
                           _isViewingSelf + role-scope rules in one check). *@
                        @if (CanActivate())
                        {
                            @if (_user.IsActive)
                            {
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionDeactivate"]"
                                              Icon="block"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                              Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                              Click="@HandleDeactivateAsync"
                                              Style="width: 100%;" />
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionActivate"]"
                                              Icon="check_circle"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Success"
                                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                              Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                              Click="@HandleActivateAsync"
                                              Style="width: 100%;" />
                            }
                        }

                        @* Reset password — Admin only (not self — confusing UX
                           even though the handler allows self-reset). *@
                        @if (_isAdmin && !_isViewingSelf)
                        {
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionResetPassword"]"
                                          Icon="vpn_key"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Warning"
                                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                          Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                          Click="@HandleResetPasswordAsync"
                                          Style="width: 100%;" />
                        }

                        @* Help panel — explains what each action does. *@
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["HelpPanelTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="font-weight: 600;" />
                        <ul class="help-list">
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_EditFullName"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_AssignRole"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_RemoveRole"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_AssignGroup"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_RemoveGroup"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_Activate"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_Deactivate"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_ResetPassword"]</li>
                        </ul>
                    </RadzenStack>
                </RadzenCard>
            </div>
        </div>
    }

    @* ── Edit Full Name modal ──
       Inline modal dialog for editing the user's FullName. Replaces the
       previous JS prompt() implementation — gives us proper labels,
       inline validation messaging, and styled Save/Cancel buttons.

       WHY INLINE MODAL (not Radzen DialogService.OpenAsync):
         - No separate .razor component file needed for a 2-field form.
         - State stays in this component (no callback marshaling).
         - Styling is consistent with the rest of the page (Radzen cards
           + RadzenTextBox + RadzenButton).
         - Focus management: the RadzenTextBox autofocuses when the modal
           opens. Escape key closes the modal (handled by the inline
           @onkeydown on the overlay).

       ACCESSIBILITY:
         - role="dialog" + aria-modal="true" on the dialog panel.
         - aria-labelledby points to the modal title.
         - Overlay click closes the modal (matches Radzen Dialog behavior).
         - Escape key closes the modal. *@
    @if (_isEditNameModalOpen)
    {
        <div class="modal-overlay" @onclick="CloseEditNameModal" role="presentation">
            <div class="modal-dialog"
                 role="dialog"
                 aria-modal="true"
                 aria-labelledby="edit-name-modal-title"
                 @onclick:stopPropagation="true"
                 @onkeydown="HandleEditNameModalKeydownAsync">
                <div class="modal-header">
                    <h2 id="edit-name-modal-title" class="modal-title">@Loc["EditNameModalTitle"]</h2>
                    <button type="button"
                            class="modal-close-btn"
                            title="@Loc["ModalCancel"]"
                            aria-label="@Loc["ModalCancel"]"
                            disabled="@_isBusy"
                            @onclick="CloseEditNameModal">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p class="modal-body-text">@Loc["EditNameModalBody"]</p>

                    <label class="modal-label" for="edit-name-input">@Loc["ColFullName"]</label>
                    <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_editNameInput"
                                   id="edit-name-input"
                                   Placeholder="@Loc["EditNameModalPlaceholder"]"
                                   Style="width: 100%;"
                                   Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                   autocomplete="off"
                                   autofocus />
                    @* Live region for inline validation — populated by
                       ValidateEditNameInput(). Announced to screen readers. *@
                    <div class="modal-validation" role="status" aria-live="polite">
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_editNameError))
                        {
                            <span class="modal-validation-error">@_editNameError</span>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="modal-footer">
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ModalCancel"]"
                                  Icon="close"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                  Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                  Click="@CloseEditNameModal" />
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ModalSave"]"
                                  Icon="save"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                  Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                  Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                  Click="@ConfirmEditNameAsync" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    }

    @* ── Reset Password modal ──
       Inline modal dialog for resetting the user's password. Same visual
       structure as the Edit FullName modal above (overlay + dialog +
       header/body/footer). Adds a show/hide password toggle (mirrors
       CreateUser.razor's password field pattern) and inline validation
       messaging.

       Admin-only (the button that opens this modal is gated by
       `_isAdmin && !_isViewingSelf`). The handler enforces
       [RequireRoles(Admin)] server-side as defense-in-depth, and Identity's
       password-complexity rules are the final authority on what's accepted. *@
    @if (_isResetPasswordModalOpen)
    {
        <div class="modal-overlay" @onclick="CloseResetPasswordModal" role="presentation">
            <div class="modal-dialog"
                 role="dialog"
                 aria-modal="true"
                 aria-labelledby="reset-password-modal-title"
                 @onclick:stopPropagation="true"
                 @onkeydown="HandleResetPasswordModalKeydownAsync">
                <div class="modal-header">
                    <h2 id="reset-password-modal-title" class="modal-title">@Loc["ResetPasswordModalTitle"]</h2>
                    <button type="button"
                            class="modal-close-btn"
                            title="@Loc["ModalCancel"]"
                            aria-label="@Loc["ModalCancel"]"
                            disabled="@_isBusy"
                            @onclick="CloseResetPasswordModal">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p class="modal-body-text">@Loc["ResetPasswordModalBody"]</p>

                    <label class="modal-label" for="reset-password-input">@Loc["ResetPasswordModalLabel"]</label>
                    <div class="modal-password-row">
                        <RadzenTextBox Value="_resetPasswordInput"
                                       ValueChanged="@OnResetPasswordChanged"
                                       id="reset-password-input"
                                       Type="@(_showResetPassword ? "text" : "password")"
                                       Placeholder="@Loc["ResetPasswordModalPlaceholder"]"
                                       Class="modal-password-field"
                                       Style="width: 100%;"
                                       Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                       autocomplete="new-password"
                                       autofocus />
                        <RadzenButton Icon="@(_showResetPassword ? "visibility_off" : "visibility")"
                                      title="@(_showResetPassword ? Loc["PasswordHide"] : Loc["PasswordShow"])"
                                      aria-label="@(_showResetPassword ? Loc["PasswordHide"] : Loc["PasswordShow"])"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                      Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                      Click="@ToggleResetPasswordVisibility" />
                    </div>
                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                        @Loc["ResetPasswordModalHint"]
                    </RadzenText>
                    <div class="modal-validation" role="status" aria-live="polite">
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_resetPasswordError))
                        {
                            <span class="modal-validation-error">@_resetPasswordError</span>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="modal-footer">
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ModalCancel"]"
                                  Icon="close"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                  Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                  Click="@CloseResetPasswordModal" />
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ResetPasswordModalSubmit"]"
                                  Icon="vpn_key"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Warning"
                                  Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                  Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                  Click="@ConfirmResetPasswordAsync" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Route parameter ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// User ID from the route (/Admin/Users/{Id:guid}). Bound by the Blazor
    /// router. Invalid Guid values trigger the router's NotFound template.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Guid Id { get; set; }

    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private UserDto? _user;
    private string? _loadError;
    private bool _isLoading = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user is in the Admin role. Computed via
    /// AuthenticationStateProvider in OnInitializedAsync — NOT via
    /// ICurrentUserService.IsInRole (which returns false over the SignalR
    /// circuit because HttpContext is null). Gates role-management UI
    /// (Assign/Remove role buttons). The Wolverine handlers also enforce
    /// [RequireRoles(Admin)] server-side as defense-in-depth.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isAdmin;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user is in the Manager role. Combined with
    /// _isAdmin to gate FullName editing and the group-remove button
    /// (both commands have [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isManager;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user is in the Employee role (and NOT also in
    /// the Admin or Manager roles). Used to gate the change-group button's
    /// Employee scope (Customer targets only) and to show the Employee-
    /// scope informational alert in the action panel. Admins and Managers
    /// who happen to also be in the Employee role are treated as
    /// Admin/Manager respectively (broader scope), so we explicitly check
    /// `!_isAdmin && !_isManager` here. Same pattern as AdminUsers.razor's
    /// _isEmployeeOnly field (Phase 6.5).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isEmployee;

    /// <summary>
    /// The current user's Domain User Id (from the "UserId" claim set by
    /// our custom IClaimsPrincipalFactory in Infrastructure). Used to hide
    /// self-Admin-removal (handler also rejects this, but hiding the button
    /// is better UX — same pattern as AdminUsers.razor hiding self-Deactivate).
    /// </summary>
    private Guid _currentUserId;

    /// <summary>
    /// True while any action (Edit FullName / Assign Role / Remove Role /
    /// Change Group / Remove Group / Activate / Deactivate / Reset Password)
    /// is in flight. Disables ALL action buttons to prevent double-clicks.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isBusy;

    /// <summary>
    /// Inline error message for the action panel. Populated when an action
    /// fails (e.g. "User '...' was not found."). Cleared at the start of
    /// the next action by ExecuteActionAsync.
    /// </summary>
    private string _actionError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The role selected in the "Assign role" dropdown. Bound via
    /// @bind-Value (two-way) — RadzenDropDown with TValue=string (primitive
    /// key, matches AdminUsers.razor's activity-filter pattern, NOT the
    /// complex-object binding that bit us in CreateUser.razor Phase 6.2).
    /// Reset to null after a successful Assign.
    /// </summary>
    private string? _selectedRoleToAdd;

    /// <summary>
    /// The list of role constants available for assignment. Computed in
    /// OnInitializedAsync and recomputed after each successful role
    /// Add/Remove (because the list excludes roles the user already has).
    /// Customer is intentionally excluded — Customer is implicit (set at
    /// creation time, not assignable post-creation from this UI).
    ///
    /// WHY List&lt;string&gt; (not List&lt;RoleOption&gt;):
    ///   The previous implementation used a complex RoleOption class with
    ///   Value + Label properties, paired with RadzenDropDown's
    ///   TextProperty="Label" + ValueProperty="Value". That triggered a
    ///   Radzen 11.1.7 bug: when TValue is a primitive (string) and Data
    ///   is a list of complex objects, SelectItem falls back to
    ///   item.ToString() instead of respecting ValueProperty, producing
    ///   the garbage label "TakOne.WebUI.Components.Pages.UserDetail+RoleOption"
    ///   in the dropdown and throwing InvalidCastException on click.
    ///
    ///   Switching to List&lt;string&gt; (raw role constants) eliminates the
    ///   cast entirely — the dropdown value IS the role string. An
    ///   ItemTemplate in the markup renders the localized label via
    ///   GetRoleLabel(roleName), so the user still sees translated text.
    /// </summary>
    private List<string> _assignableRoles = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// All staff-role options (excludes Customer) used to build the
    /// assignable-roles list. The 4 staff roles match the AllowedStaffRoles
    /// set on CreateStaffCommandValidator.
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly string[] StaffRoles =
        { Roles.Admin, Roles.Manager, Roles.Employee, Roles.ReadOnly };

    // ── Edit Full Name modal state ────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// True when the Edit FullName modal is open. Toggled by
    /// HandleEditFullNameAsync (open) and CloseEditNameModal/ConfirmEditNameAsync
    /// (close). When true, the modal markup at the bottom of the file renders
    /// above all other content via position:fixed + z-index.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isEditNameModalOpen;

    /// <summary>
    /// The text currently typed into the modal's RadzenTextBox. Two-way
    /// bound via @bind-Value. Pre-filled with the user's current FullName
    /// when the modal opens (in HandleEditFullNameAsync). Validated by
    /// ValidateEditNameInput before dispatching the command.
    /// </summary>
    private string _editNameInput = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Inline validation message shown below the modal's text box. Cleared
    /// on every input change (Blazor @bind-Value re-renders) and re-populated
    /// by ValidateEditNameInput when Save is clicked. Empty string = no error.
    /// </summary>
    private string _editNameError = string.Empty;

    // ── Reset Password modal state ────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// True when the Reset Password modal is open. Toggled by
    /// HandleResetPasswordAsync (open) and CloseResetPasswordModal/
    /// ConfirmResetPasswordAsync (close). Mirrors the Edit FullName modal's
    /// state pattern.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isResetPasswordModalOpen;

    /// <summary>
    /// The new password currently typed into the modal's RadzenTextBox.
    /// Updated via the ValueChanged callback (NOT @bind-Value — see
    /// OnResetPasswordChanged remark). Cleared when the modal closes.
    /// </summary>
    private string _resetPasswordInput = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Inline validation message shown below the modal's password box.
    /// Populated by ValidateResetPasswordInput when Submit is clicked.
    /// Empty string = no error.
    /// </summary>
    private string _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Toggles the password box between masked (default) and plaintext.
    /// Mirrors CreateUser.razor's _showPassword pattern. Purely a UX
    /// affordance — no validation implications.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _showResetPassword;

    // ── Change group panel state (Phase 6.6) ─────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// True when the inline Change Group panel is expanded (the user
    /// clicked the green "Change group" / "Assign to group" button).
    /// When true, the Group card shows the Existing/New toggle + the
    /// corresponding picker + Save/Cancel buttons. When false, the card
    /// shows just the current group + the green button.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isChangeGroupPanelOpen;

    /// <summary>
    /// Group name UI mode — mirrors CreateUser.razor's GroupMode enum.
    /// Existing = pick from the list of available groups (loaded via
    /// GetAllGroupNamesQuery). New = type a new group name in a text box.
    /// See the _pendingGroupName field remark for the selection flow.
    /// </summary>
    private GroupMode _groupMode = GroupMode.Existing;

    /// <summary>
    /// The pending group name selection/entry. In Existing mode, this is
    /// set by clicking one of the group buttons (SelectExistingGroup).
    /// In New mode, this is bound to the textbox via @bind-Value. Reset
    /// when the panel opens, when the mode changes, or when the panel
    /// closes (saved or cancelled).
    /// </summary>
    private string _pendingGroupName = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The list of existing customer group names, loaded once on page
    /// init from GetAllGroupNamesQuery. Rendered as a 2-column grid of
    /// selectable cards when the change-group panel is open in Existing
    /// mode. Mirrors CreateUser.razor's _availableGroups field.
    /// </summary>
    private List<string> _availableGroups = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// Group name UI mode (mirrors CreateUser.razor's GroupMode enum).
    /// Existing = pick from the list of available groups. New = type a
    /// new group name in a text box. See _groupMode field.
    /// </summary>
    private enum GroupMode { Existing, New }

    // ── Derived permission flags ───────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user can edit FullName (matches
    /// UpdateUserFullNameCommand's [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canEditFullName => _isAdmin || _isManager;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user can manage roles (matches
    /// AssignUserRoleCommand + RemoveUserRoleCommand's [RequireRoles(Admin)]).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canManageRoles => _isAdmin;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the viewer is looking at their OWN user detail page
    /// (_currentUserId == _user.Id). Used to gate self-role-management
    /// UI (admins cannot assign/remove roles on themselves from this
    /// page — they need another admin to do it) and self-activate/
    /// deactivate (handler rejects self-activation too). The backend
    /// handlers ALSO reject self-Admin-removal and self-activation as
    /// defense-in-depth.
    ///
    /// WHY THIS EXISTS:
    ///   Admins CAN change the roles of OTHER admins (including removing
    ///   Admin from another admin). They CANNOT modify their OWN roles
    ///   from this page. Previously, the only protection was the backend
    ///   rejecting self-Admin-removal — but the UI still showed the
    ///   dropdown and Remove buttons, which led to confused clicks and
    ///   error toasts. Now the entire role-management UI is hidden when
    ///   _isViewingSelf is true, replaced with an info alert.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isViewingSelf => _user is not null && _currentUserId == _user.Id;

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns true if the current viewer may activate/deactivate the user
    /// currently loaded on this page. Mirrors the server-side scope rules
    /// enforced by ActivateUserCommandHandler / DeactivateUserCommandHandler.
    ///
    /// Rules (per user spec, Phase 6.6):
    ///   - Admin    → anyone EXCEPT self (handler also rejects self).
    ///   - Manager  → target must be Employee or Customer, AND must NOT be
    ///                self, Manager, or Admin.
    ///   - Employee → cannot activate/deactivate anyone (the command is
    ///                [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)] — Employees are
    ///                rejected by the auth middleware before the handler
    ///                even runs).
    ///
    /// Returns false for _isViewingSelf regardless of role (the handler
    /// rejects self-activation with "You cannot activate yourself. You
    /// are already active.").
    /// </summary>
    private bool CanActivate()
    {
        if (_user is null) return false;
        if (_isViewingSelf) return false;

        // Admins can activate/deactivate anyone except self (already checked).
        if (_isAdmin) return true;

        // Managers can activate/deactivate Employee or Customer targets,
        // but NOT other managers, admins, or read-onlys.
        if (_isManager && !_isAdmin)
        {
            var targetIsManager = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Manager);
            var targetIsAdmin = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Admin);
            var targetIsEmployeeOrCustomer = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Employee)
                                          || _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Customer);
            return !targetIsManager && !targetIsAdmin && targetIsEmployeeOrCustomer;
        }

        // Employees (and anyone else) — cannot activate/deactivate anyone.
        return false;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns true if the current viewer may change the group of the user
    /// currently loaded on this page. Mirrors the server-side scope rules
    /// enforced by AssignUserToGroupCommandHandler.
    ///
    /// Rules (per user spec, Phase 6.6):
    ///   - Admin    → anyone (including self, though admins don't have groups
    ///                — but the handler permits it).
    ///   - Manager  → target must be Employee or Customer, AND must NOT be
    ///                self, Manager, or Admin.
    ///   - Employee → target must be Customer, AND must NOT be self,
    ///                Employee, Manager, or Admin.
    ///
    /// Multi-role interpretation (matches the handler):
    ///   - A Manager+Employee target is treated as "another manager" and
    ///     is off-limits to Manager callers.
    ///   - A Customer+Employee target is treated as "another employee" and
    ///     is off-limits to Employee callers.
    /// </summary>
    private bool CanChangeGroup()
    {
        if (_user is null) return false;

        // Admins can change anyone's group.
        if (_isAdmin) return true;

        // Self-check: Managers and Employees cannot change their own group.
        if (_isViewingSelf) return false;

        if (_isManager && !_isAdmin)
        {
            // Manager scope: target must be Employee or Customer, AND must
            // NOT be Manager or Admin.
            var targetIsManager = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Manager);
            var targetIsAdmin = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Admin);
            var targetIsEmployeeOrCustomer = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Employee)
                                          || _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Customer);
            return !targetIsManager && !targetIsAdmin && targetIsEmployeeOrCustomer;
        }

        if (_isEmployee && !_isAdmin && !_isManager)
        {
            // Employee scope: target must be Customer, AND must NOT be
            // Employee, Manager, or Admin.
            var targetIsEmployee = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Employee);
            var targetIsManager = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Manager);
            var targetIsAdmin = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Admin);
            var targetIsCustomer = _user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Customer);
            return !targetIsEmployee && !targetIsManager && !targetIsAdmin && targetIsCustomer;
        }

        // Anyone else — deny.
        return false;
    }

    // ── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Compute _isAdmin, _isManager, _currentUserId synchronously via
        // AuthStateProvider so the action-stack visibility doesn't flicker
        // on first render. NOTE: we deliberately do NOT use
        // ICurrentUserService.IsInRole here — in interactive Blazor Server
        // mode, ICurrentUserService resolves from IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext,
        // which is null over the SignalR circuit (only populated during the
        // initial prerender). The AuthStateProvider is the canonical source
        // for interactive components. The Wolverine command handlers also
        // enforce [RequireRoles] server-side (defense-in-depth).
        try
        {
            var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
            var user = authState.User;

            if (user?.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
            {
                // The UserId claim is set by our custom IClaimsPrincipalFactory
                // in the Infrastructure layer — it's the Domain User's Guid Id.
                // Fallback to NameIdentifier for safety (same claim-resolution
                // pattern as AdminUsers.razor lines 522-523).
                var idClaim = user.FindFirst("UserId")?.Value
                              ?? user.FindFirst(System.Security.Claims.ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;
                if (Guid.TryParse(idClaim, out var parsedId))
                {
                    _currentUserId = parsedId;
                }

                _isAdmin = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin);
                _isManager = user.IsInRole(Roles.Manager);
                // Employee-only means "in Employee role AND not also Admin
                // or Manager". Admins and Managers who happen to also be
                // in the Employee role are treated as Admin/Manager
                // respectively (broader scope). This field gates the
                // change-group button's Employee scope (customers only)
                // and the Employee-scope informational alert.
                _isEmployee = !_isAdmin && !_isManager && user.IsInRole(Roles.Employee);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Non-fatal — _currentUserId stays Guid.Empty (no self-action
            // buttons hidden, which is safe but slightly worse UX) and
            // _isAdmin/_isManager/_isEmployee stay false (all action UI
            // hidden — safer fallback if role resolution fails). The
            // handler still enforces [RequireRoles] server-side.
        }

        try
        {
            // Load existing customer group names in parallel with the user
            // (so the change-group panel doesn't have to wait when opened).
            // Non-fatal on failure — _availableGroups stays empty, which
            // just means the Existing mode shows "No existing groups" and
            // the user has to use the New mode.
            try
            {
                var groupsResult = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<List<string>>>(
                    new GetAllGroupNamesQuery());

                if (groupsResult.IsSuccess && groupsResult.Value is not null)
                {
                    _availableGroups = groupsResult.Value
                        .Where(g => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(g))
                        .OrderBy(g => g)
                        .ToList();
                }
            }
            catch
            {
                // Non-fatal — see comment above.
                _availableGroups = new List<string>();
            }

            await LoadUserAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadUserAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = null;

        try
        {
            await LoadUserCoreAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Silent-reload variant used by ExecuteActionAsync after a successful
    /// action. Skips toggling _isLoading so the page doesn't flash the
    /// full-page loading spinner between a successful action and the
    /// refreshed content. Mirrors the pattern SaleDetail.razor would use
    /// if it had been written with this concern in mind (a P2 soft-issue
    /// noted in phase-6.3-static-review — fixed here so UserDetail doesn't
    /// inherit the SaleDetail quirk).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ReloadUserSilentlyAsync()
    {
        // NOTE: do NOT touch _isLoading here — that would blank the page
        // with the loading spinner. We keep _isBusy = true (set by the
        // caller ExecuteActionAsync) so action buttons stay disabled while
        // the reload is in flight.
        try
        {
            await LoadUserCoreAsync();
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            // Silent-reload failures are non-fatal — the action itself
            // already succeeded and we already toasted success. The next
            // user interaction (or a manual page refresh) will surface
            // any persistent load failure via the regular LoadUserAsync
            // path. Logging would be nice but this is a UI-layer catch.
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Shared core for both LoadUserAsync (initial load + retry) and
    /// ReloadUserSilentlyAsync (post-action refresh). Sets _user + _loadError
    /// + refreshes the assignable-roles dropdown. Does NOT touch _isLoading —
    /// that's the caller's responsibility.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadUserCoreAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var query = new GetUserByIdQuery { UserId = Id };
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<UserDto>>(query);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _user = result.Value;
                _loadError = null;
                RefreshAssignableRoles();
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains the handler's user-friendly message.
                // For "not found" (covers both genuinely-missing AND
                // permission-denied), we show the same NotFound UI.
                _loadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
                _user = null;
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
            _user = null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Rebuilds the assignable-roles list, excluding roles the user
    /// already has. Called after every successful Load (initial + reload
    /// after each action) so the dropdown never shows already-assigned
    /// roles. Customer is intentionally never in this list.
    /// </summary>
    private void RefreshAssignableRoles()
    {
        if (_user is null)
        {
            _assignableRoles = new();
            return;
        }

        // Build a list of raw role constants (List<string>) — the
        // dropdown's ItemTemplate will render the localized label via
        // GetRoleLabel(roleName). See the _assignableRoles field remark
        // for why we don't use a complex RoleOption class anymore.
        _assignableRoles = StaffRoles
            .Where(r => !_user.Roles.Contains(r))
            .ToList();

        // If the previously-selected role is no longer assignable (because
        // the user just got assigned it), clear the selection.
        if (_selectedRoleToAdd is not null
            && !_assignableRoles.Contains(_selectedRoleToAdd))
        {
            _selectedRoleToAdd = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Actions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    // ── Edit Full Name modal handlers ──

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the Edit FullName modal. Pre-fills the input with the user's
    /// current FullName and clears any previous validation error. Called
    /// from the "Edit name" buttons in the profile card and the action
    /// panel.
    ///
    /// REPLACES the previous JS prompt() implementation — the modal gives
    /// us proper labels, inline validation messaging, styled Save/Cancel
    /// buttons, and consistent styling with the rest of the page. See the
    /// modal markup at the bottom of this file for the dialog structure.
    /// </summary>
    private void HandleEditFullNameAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_canEditFullName) return;

        _editNameInput = _user.FullName;
        _editNameError = string.Empty;
        _isEditNameModalOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Closes the Edit FullName modal without saving. Called by:
    ///   - The Cancel button
    ///   - The X close button in the modal header
    ///   - Clicking outside the dialog (on the overlay)
    ///   - Pressing Escape (via HandleEditNameModalKeydownAsync)
    /// Silent — no toast (the user explicitly chose not to save).
    /// </summary>
    private void CloseEditNameModal()
    {
        // Don't allow closing while a save is in flight — prevents
        // orphaned state if the user clicks Cancel mid-dispatch.
        if (_isBusy) return;

        _isEditNameModalOpen = false;
        _editNameInput = string.Empty;
        _editNameError = string.Empty;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Keydown handler for the modal dialog. Closes the modal on Escape
    /// (matches standard modal behavior across OSes). Other keys are
    /// ignored. Wired via @onkeydown on the .modal-dialog div.
    /// </summary>
    private Task HandleEditNameModalKeydownAsync(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
        if (e?.Key == "Escape" && !_isBusy)
        {
            CloseEditNameModal();
        }
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Validates the modal's _editNameInput. Returns true if valid (and
    /// populates _editNameError for inline display if invalid).
    /// Mirrors the server-side validator:
    ///   - Non-empty after trim
    ///   - ≤ 200 chars (UpdateUserFullNameCommandValidator.MaxFullNameLength)
    /// </summary>
    private bool ValidateEditNameInput()
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_editNameInput))
        {
            _editNameError = Loc["EditNameRequiredError"];
            return false;
        }

        var trimmed = _editNameInput.Trim();
        if (trimmed.Length > 200)
        {
            _editNameError = Loc["FullNameLengthError"];
            return false;
        }

        _editNameError = string.Empty;
        return true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Save handler for the Edit FullName modal. Validates the input; if
    /// valid, dispatches UpdateUserFullNameCommand via ExecuteActionAsync
    /// (which toasts success/failure and reloads the user). On success,
    /// the modal closes. On validation failure, the modal stays open and
    /// the inline error is shown.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ConfirmEditNameAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_canEditFullName) return;

        if (!ValidateEditNameInput()) return;

        var newName = _editNameInput.Trim();

        // Close the modal IMMEDIATELY so the user sees acknowledgment of
        // their click — the actual save happens via ExecuteActionAsync,
        // which sets _isBusy (disabling action buttons). The modal's
        // own _isBusy guard prevents double-clicks during the brief
        // window between modal-close and _isBusy=true.
        _isEditNameModalOpen = false;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionEditFullName"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new UpdateUserFullNameCommand(_user.Id, newName)));

        // Clear the input after the action completes (success or failure
        // — either way, the modal is closed and the input is stale).
        _editNameInput = string.Empty;
        _editNameError = string.Empty;
    }

    // ── Other action handlers ──

    /// <summary>
    /// Assign the currently-selected role (_selectedRoleToAdd) to the user.
    /// The dropdown is filtered to exclude already-assigned roles, so this
    /// should always be a new role — but the handler/validator is the
    /// final authority server-side. Also rejects self-assignment
    /// defensively (the markup hides the entire Assign UI on self-view).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleAssignRoleAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_canManageRoles) return;
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(_selectedRoleToAdd)) return;

        // Defense-in-depth: the markup hides ALL role-management UI when
        // _isViewingSelf is true. If a stale render or crafty click slips
        // through, refuse to act on self.
        if (_isViewingSelf)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["CannotModifyOwnRolesBody"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionAssignRole"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new AssignUserRoleCommand(_user.Id, _selectedRoleToAdd)));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Remove a specific role from the user. Hidden entirely when the
    /// viewer is on their own page (the markup guards _isViewingSelf),
    /// but this handler also rejects self-removal defensively in case
    /// the markup is bypassed. The backend handler rejects self-Admin-
    /// removal as a third line of defense.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleRemoveRoleAsync(string role)
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_canManageRoles) return;
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(role)) return;

        // Defense-in-depth: the markup hides ALL role-management UI when
        // _isViewingSelf is true, but if a stale render or a crafty click
        // somehow reaches this handler, we refuse to act on self.
        if (_isViewingSelf)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["CannotModifyOwnRolesBody"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        // Belt-and-suspenders: the markup also hides this button, but the
        // check is cheap and the handler also rejects it. We don't want to
        // even attempt the dispatch.
        if (_currentUserId == _user.Id && role == Roles.Admin)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["CannotRemoveOwnAdminRole"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        // JS confirm() — role removal is reversible (re-assign) but worth
        // one click of friction so the admin doesn't accidentally lock
        // themselves or another user out of a feature.
        var confirmMessage = string.Format(
            CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
            Loc["ConfirmRemoveRole"],
            GetRoleLabel(role),
            _user.FullName);

        var confirmed = await JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("confirm", confirmMessage);
        if (!confirmed) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionRemoveRole"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new RemoveUserRoleCommand(_user.Id, role)));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the inline Change Group panel. Pre-selects Existing mode and
    /// clears any pending group name. Called when the user clicks the green
    /// "Change group" / "Assign to group" button on the Group card.
    /// </summary>
    private Task OpenChangeGroupPanel()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !CanChangeGroup()) return Task.CompletedTask;

        // If no existing groups exist, default to New mode so the user isn't
        // stuck staring at "No existing groups" with no recourse (same UX as
        // CreateUser.razor's OnInitializedAsync fallback).
        _groupMode = _availableGroups.Count == 0 ? GroupMode.New : GroupMode.Existing;
        _pendingGroupName = string.Empty;
        _isChangeGroupPanelOpen = true;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Closes the inline Change Group panel without saving. Clears the
    /// pending group name and resets the mode to Existing (the default).
    /// </summary>
    private Task CancelChangeGroup()
    {
        if (_isBusy) return Task.CompletedTask;

        _isChangeGroupPanelOpen = false;
        _pendingGroupName = string.Empty;
        _groupMode = GroupMode.Existing;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Switches between Existing and New group-name modes. Clears the
    /// pending group name so the user must explicitly pick or type one in
    /// the new mode. Mirrors CreateUser.razor's OnGroupModeChanged.
    /// </summary>
    private Task OnGroupModeChanged(GroupMode newMode)
    {
        if (_isBusy) return Task.CompletedTask;
        if (_groupMode == newMode) return Task.CompletedTask;

        _groupMode = newMode;
        _pendingGroupName = string.Empty;  // force fresh selection/entry
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Sets the pending group name to the given existing-group name. Called
    /// when the user clicks one of the group buttons in Existing mode. Only
    /// one group can be selected at a time — clicking a different button
    /// overwrites the pending selection. Mirrors CreateUser.razor's
    /// SelectExistingGroup.
    /// </summary>
    private Task SelectExistingGroup(string groupName)
    {
        if (_isBusy) return Task.CompletedTask;
        _pendingGroupName = groupName;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Save handler for the inline Change Group panel. Validates the pending
    /// group name; if valid, dispatches AssignUserToGroupCommand via
    /// ExecuteActionAsync (which toasts success/failure and reloads the
    /// user). On success, the panel closes. On validation failure, the panel
    /// stays open and the inline error is shown via toast.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ConfirmChangeGroupAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !CanChangeGroup()) return;

        // Defense-in-depth: the Save button is disabled when the pending
        // name is empty, but this check guards against a race.
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_pendingGroupName))
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["GroupNameLengthError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        var groupName = _pendingGroupName.Trim();

        if (groupName.Length > 100)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["GroupNameLengthError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        // Close the panel IMMEDIATELY so the user sees acknowledgment —
        // the actual save happens via ExecuteActionAsync, which sets
        // _isBusy (disabling action buttons).
        _isChangeGroupPanelOpen = false;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionChangeGroup"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new AssignUserToGroupCommand(_user.Id, groupName)));

        // Clear pending state after the action completes (success or
        // failure — either way, the panel is closed).
        _pendingGroupName = string.Empty;
        _groupMode = GroupMode.Existing;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Remove the user from their current group. Uses JS confirm() because
    /// removing a customer from their group affects their purchase limits.
    /// Only callable by Admin/Manager (the button is hidden from Employees
    /// — RemoveUserFromGroupCommand is [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleRemoveGroupAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy) return;
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName)) return;
        if (!(_isAdmin || _isManager)) return;  // defense-in-depth

        var confirmMessage = string.Format(
            CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
            Loc["ConfirmRemoveGroup"],
            _user.GroupName,
            _user.FullName);

        var confirmed = await JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("confirm", confirmMessage);
        if (!confirmed) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionRemoveGroup"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new RemoveUserFromGroupCommand(_user.Id)));
    }

    // ── Activate / Deactivate handlers (Phase 6.6) ───────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Activate the user. No confirmation dialog — activation is a
    /// non-destructive restore. The handler rejects self-activation as
    /// defense-in-depth (the button is also hidden on self-view via
    /// CanActivate). Mirrors AdminUsers.razor's HandleActivateAsync.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleActivateAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !CanActivate()) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionActivate"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new ActivateUserCommand(_user.Id)));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Deactivate the user. Uses JS confirm() — deactivation is reversible
    /// (re-activate) but worth one click of friction. The handler rejects
    /// self-deactivation as defense-in-depth (the button is also hidden on
    /// self-view via CanActivate). Mirrors AdminUsers.razor's
    /// HandleDeactivateAsync.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleDeactivateAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !CanActivate()) return;

        var confirmMessage = string.Format(
            CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
            Loc["ConfirmDeactivate"],
            _user.FullName,
            _user.WorkerId);

        var confirmed = await JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("confirm", confirmMessage);
        if (!confirmed) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionDeactivate"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new DeactivateUserCommand(_user.Id)));
    }

    // ── Reset Password modal handlers (Phase 6.6) ────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the Reset Password modal. Clears any previous input + error.
    /// Called from the "Reset password" button in the action panel (Admin
    /// only, not self).
    /// </summary>
    private void HandleResetPasswordAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_isAdmin || _isViewingSelf) return;

        _resetPasswordInput = string.Empty;
        _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;
        _showResetPassword = false;
        _isResetPasswordModalOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Closes the Reset Password modal without saving. Called by the Cancel
    /// button, the X close button, overlay click, or Escape key. Silent —
    /// no toast (the user explicitly chose not to save).
    /// </summary>
    private void CloseResetPasswordModal()
    {
        // Don't allow closing while a save is in flight.
        if (_isBusy) return;

        _isResetPasswordModalOpen = false;
        _resetPasswordInput = string.Empty;
        _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;
        _showResetPassword = false;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Keydown handler for the Reset Password modal. Closes the modal on
    /// Escape (matches the Edit FullName modal's behavior).
    /// </summary>
    private Task HandleResetPasswordModalKeydownAsync(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
        if (e?.Key == "Escape" && !_isBusy)
        {
            CloseResetPasswordModal();
        }
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Bound to the password box's ValueChanged callback so we can toggle
    /// the input type between Text and Password without losing the value
    /// (using @bind-Value with a type change can drop the current input).
    /// Same pattern as CreateUser.razor's OnPasswordChanged.
    /// </summary>
    private Task OnResetPasswordChanged(string value)
    {
        _resetPasswordInput = value ?? string.Empty;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Toggles the password visibility between masked and plaintext.
    /// Purely a UX affordance — no validation implications. Mirrors
    /// CreateUser.razor's TogglePasswordVisibility.
    /// </summary>
    private Task ToggleResetPasswordVisibility()
    {
        _showResetPassword = !_showResetPassword;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Validates _resetPasswordInput. Returns true if valid (and populates
    /// _resetPasswordError for inline display if invalid). Minimal client-
    /// side check — Identity's complexity rules are the real authority and
    /// will reject anything too weak server-side.
    /// </summary>
    private bool ValidateResetPasswordInput()
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_resetPasswordInput))
        {
            _resetPasswordError = Loc["ResetPasswordRequiredError"];
            return false;
        }

        if (_resetPasswordInput.Length < 8)
        {
            _resetPasswordError = Loc["ResetPasswordLengthError"];
            return false;
        }

        _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;
        return true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Submit handler for the Reset Password modal. Validates the input; if
    /// valid, dispatches ResetUserPasswordCommand via ExecuteActionAsync.
    /// On success, the modal closes. On validation failure, the modal stays
    /// open and the inline error is shown.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ConfirmResetPasswordAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_isAdmin || _isViewingSelf) return;

        if (!ValidateResetPasswordInput()) return;

        var newPassword = _resetPasswordInput;

        // Close the modal IMMEDIATELY so the user sees acknowledgment.
        _isResetPasswordModalOpen = false;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionResetPassword"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new ResetUserPasswordCommand(_user.Id, newPassword)));

        // Clear the input after the action completes (success or failure).
        _resetPasswordInput = string.Empty;
        _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;
        _showResetPassword = false;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Common wrapper for all actions (Edit FullName / Assign Role /
    /// Remove Role / Change Group / Remove Group / Activate / Deactivate /
    /// Reset Password): sets _isBusy, clears the previous _actionError,
    /// dispatches the command, handles success (toast + reload the user to
    /// refresh roles/group/FullName/IsActive) and failure (inline
    /// _actionError banner + error toast). Mirrors SaleDetail.razor's
    /// ExecuteActionAsync pattern exactly.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ExecuteActionAsync(string actionName, Func<Task<Result>> dispatch)
    {
        _isBusy = true;
        _actionError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            var result = await dispatch();

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActionSuccessFormat"], actionName),
                    summary: Loc["ActionSuccessTitle"]);

                // Reload the user to refresh the roles list, group badge,
                // and FullName display. Also rebuilds the assignable-roles
                // dropdown (excludes the just-assigned role, or restores
                // the just-removed role). Uses the SILENT variant so the
                // page doesn't flash the full-page loading spinner between
                // the toast and the refreshed content.
                await ReloadUserSilentlyAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains the handler's user-friendly message
                // (e.g. "User '...' was not found.", or "You cannot remove
                // your own Admin role. Assign Admin to another user first.").
                _actionError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericAction"];
                await Toast.Error(_actionError, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _actionError = Loc["Error_GenericAction"];
            await Toast.Error(_actionError, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusy = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Display helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns the localized label for a Gender enum value. Same mapping
    /// as AdminUsers.razor's GetGenderLabel (Phase 6.1) — duplicated here
    /// so the detail page is self-contained without depending on
    /// AdminUsers.resx.
    /// </summary>
    private string GetGenderLabel(Gender gender) => gender switch
    {
        Gender.Male => Loc["GenderMale"],
        Gender.Female => Loc["GenderFemale"],
        _ => gender.ToString()
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns the localized label for a role constant. Falls back to the
    /// raw role name if no translation is defined. Same mapping as
    /// CreateUser.razor's role labels.
    /// </summary>
    private string GetRoleLabel(string role) => role switch
    {
        Roles.Admin => Loc["RoleAdmin"],
        Roles.Manager => Loc["RoleManager"],
        Roles.Employee => Loc["RoleEmployee"],
        Roles.ReadOnly => Loc["RoleReadOnly"],
        Roles.Customer => Loc["RoleCustomer"],
        _ => role
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Maps a role to a Radzen BadgeStyle for color coding. Admin gets
    /// Danger (highest privilege — visually distinct). Manager gets
    /// Warning. Employee gets Info. ReadOnly gets Base. Customer gets
    /// Success (buyer role — positive connotation).
    /// </summary>
    private static BadgeStyle GetRoleBadgeStyle(string role) => role switch
    {
        Roles.Admin => BadgeStyle.Danger,
        Roles.Manager => BadgeStyle.Warning,
        Roles.Employee => BadgeStyle.Info,
        Roles.ReadOnly => BadgeStyle.Base,
        Roles.Customer => BadgeStyle.Success,
        _ => BadgeStyle.Base
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns the localized label for the current viewer's scope (shown
    /// in the action panel header). Includes Employee as a distinct scope
    /// (Phase 6.6) so Employees see their own badge rather than the
    /// generic "Viewer" label.
    /// </summary>
    private string GetScopeLabel() => _isAdmin
        ? Loc["ScopeAdmin"]
        : _isManager
            ? Loc["ScopeManager"]
            : _isEmployee
                ? Loc["ScopeEmployee"]
                : Loc["ScopeViewer"];

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a Material icon name for the current viewer's scope.
    /// </summary>
    private static string GetScopeIcon() => "shield_person";

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a CSS class for the scope badge. Admin = primary (highest
    /// privilege — visually distinct). Manager = info. Employee = a softer
    /// info shade. Anything else = base (read-only viewer).
    /// </summary>
    private string GetScopeBadgeCssClass() => _isAdmin
        ? "scope-bg-admin"
        : _isManager
            ? "scope-bg-manager"
            : _isEmployee
                ? "scope-bg-viewer"  // Employee uses the same muted gray as read-only viewers
                : "scope-bg-viewer";

    // ── Toggle helpers (Phase 6.6 — mirror CreateUser.razor) ─────────
    // Each takes a `bool selected` parameter so the SAME helpers can be
    // reused for both the Group Mode toggle (Existing / New) AND the
    // Existing-group buttons list. Same pattern as CreateUser.razor's
    // GetToggleClass / GetToggleBorderStyle / GetToggleIconStyle /
    // GetToggleTextStyle helpers.

    private static string GetToggleClass(bool selected)
    {
        return selected ? "toggle-option is-selected" : "toggle-option";
    }

    private static string GetToggleBorderStyle(bool selected)
    {
        var borderColor = selected ? "var(--rz-primary)" : "var(--rz-border-color)";
        return $"padding: 0.75rem; cursor: pointer; border: 2px solid {borderColor};";
    }

    private static string GetToggleIconStyle(bool selected)
    {
        var color = selected ? "var(--rz-primary)" : "var(--rz-text-secondary-color)";
        return $"color: {color};";
    }

    private static string GetToggleTextStyle(bool selected)
    {
        var color = selected ? "var(--rz-primary)" : "var(--rz-text-color)";
        return $"font-weight: 600; margin: 0; color: {color};";
    }
}